; regression test for `load`'s relative-path resolution (todo-claude.md's "solve the path
; puzzle, also check `load ../foo.kurt`"): a file can `load` another file in a *subdirectory*
; of its own directory, not just a sibling file. `load_file` resolves against
; `Path(filename).parent.resolve()` (the loading file's own directory) before falling back
; to `theory_path`, so a relative path with subdirectory components should just work.
load sub/inner.kurt
use R
R
